## The results

These are the numbers we measured:

| Metric | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First response | 7 h 16 min (human, average) | ~2 minutes (automated) |
| People answering chat | ~10 | 2 to 3 |

First response went from more than 7 hours to about 2 minutes. A note on the comparison: before, we measured the first human reply; now, the first automated reply. But for the customer what matters is the same: someone answers with useful information almost right away.

The support team went from about 10 people to 2 or 3. At a reference cost of US$300 per person per month, that's **more than US$2,100 per month** saved, not counting social charges or other costs tied to each position.

The people who stayed don't do the repetitive work. They handle the cases the bot passes to them: complaints, special orders, customers who prefer to talk to someone. That's more useful work than copying prices from the inventory into the chat.

